#: prompts/actions.lua:263
msgid "Explain"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:264
msgid ""
"Explains the selected passage clearly, matching the tone of the source "
"material."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:287
msgid "Quick Explain"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:288
msgid ""
"A two-or-three-sentence plain-language explanation of the selection, on a "
"fast model."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:309
msgid "ELI5"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:310
msgid ""
"Simplifies the passage into everyday language using analogies and concrete "
"examples, without sacrificing accuracy."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:325
msgid "Summarize"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:326
msgid ""
"Condenses the selected passage to its essential points, keeping what matters "
"and trimming the rest."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:341
msgid "Elaborate"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:342
msgid ""
"Expands on the passage by unpacking concepts, adding context, and exploring "
"implications."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:355
msgid ""
"Finds connections between the passage and broader themes, other works, "
"thinkers, and intellectual traditions."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:376
msgid "Connect (With Notes)"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:377
msgid ""
"Connects the passage to your own highlights and notebook entries, revealing "
"patterns and echoes in your reading. Requires annotations and notebook "
"sharing to be enabled."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:417
msgid "Explain in Context"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:418
msgid ""
"Helps you understand what a passage means: its content, context, and the "
"ideas it builds on. Comprehension-focused. Works well for longer or "
"particularly difficult passages that benefit from document context."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:449
msgid "Analyze in Context"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:450
msgid ""
"Connects the passage to your own reading: your highlights, annotations, "
"notebook entries, and the threads you've been tracking. Reader-focused, not "
"just content-focused."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:493
msgid "Thematic Connection"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:494
msgid ""
"Examines the author's craft: how language, structure, and technique achieve "
"the passage's effect, and how it fits into the work's thematic architecture."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:531
msgid "Fact Check"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:532
msgid ""
"Searches the web to verify claims in the selected passage, rating accuracy "
"and citing current sources as evidence."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:559
msgid "Counterpoint"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:560
msgid ""
"Argues against the selected passage: the strongest objections to its claim, "
"reasoning, and framing, and who would disagree. Fact Check verifies "
"accuracy; Counterpoint challenges the argument."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:587
msgid "Current Context"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:588
msgid ""
"Searches the web for the latest developments on the topic discussed in the "
"selected passage: what has changed since it was written."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:616
msgid ""
"Generates a Wikipedia-style encyclopedia entry about the selected text, "
"using AI knowledge and optionally web search for current information."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:655
msgid "Grammar"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:656
msgid ""
"Explains the grammar of the selected text in plain terms: sentence "
"structure, word roles, and anything notable."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:684
msgid ""
"Search this book's X-Ray for selected text. Local lookup: no AI call, works "
"offline."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:702
msgid "Generate Image"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:703
msgid ""
"Generate an image from the selected text description using the current AI "
"provider."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:706
msgid ""
"This action skips the chat pipeline, but it does send one AI request: the "
"framed prompt below goes to the image provider's API. Provider, model, size "
"and prompt framing are set in Settings → Advanced → Image Generation."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:722
msgid "Switch model"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:723
msgid ""
"Shows your model. Tap it to switch to a favorite, a recent pick or any other "
"model; the menu stays open. Actions with a model of their own keep it."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:727
msgid ""
"A button, not an action: it sends nothing. A pick changes your model for "
"everything after, as Settings → Model does. The highlight menu and the "
"dictionary popup can show it."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:1423
msgid ""
"Comprehensive overview: what the work is about, its themes, significance, "
"and reading experience. Based on AI knowledge: no book data needed."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:1469
msgid "Find Similar"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:1470
msgid ""
"Recommends 5-7 similar works, explaining what makes each one similar and who "
"would prefer which. When library scanning is enabled, notes which "
"recommendations you already own."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:1498
msgid "About Author"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:1499
msgid ""
"Biography, major works, writing style, and suggested reading order for the "
"author."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:1510
msgid "Historical Context"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:1511
msgid ""
"Explores when the work was written, what was happening at the time, and how "
"it reflects or responds to its era."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:1526
msgid ""
"Builds a structured reference guide (characters, themes, locations, "
"timeline) up to your current reading position, from the book text alone. "
"Completely spoiler-free. Updates incrementally as you read further. Can also "
"target a specific section from the table of contents."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:1529
msgid "Or use X-Ray (Simple) for an overview based on AI knowledge."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:1627
msgid ""
"A prose companion guide from AI knowledge: characters, themes, settings, key "
"terms. No text extraction needed. Uses reading progress to avoid spoilers."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:1713
msgid ""
"A 'Previously on...' refresher to help you get back into reading after time "
"away. Covers recent events, active threads, and where you left off. Adapts "
"to fiction or non-fiction. When highlights are shared, weaves in what you "
"found notable. Updates incrementally as you read further."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:1800 prompts/actions.lua:2355
msgid "Analyze Notes"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:1801
msgid ""
"Analyzes your note-taking and highlighting patterns to reveal what catches "
"your attention, emerging themes, and connections between your notes. This is "
"about understanding you as a reader, not summarizing the work."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:1862
msgid "Related Thinkers"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:1863
msgid ""
"Maps the intellectual landscape: who influenced the author, who the author "
"influenced, and contemporary thinkers working on similar problems. For "
"fiction, focuses on literary influences and movements."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:1899
msgid ""
"Breaks down the work's thesis, supporting arguments, evidence, assumptions, "
"and potential counterarguments. For fiction, analyzes themes and the "
"author's worldview instead. Can target a specific section. Result is saved "
"as an artifact."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:1953
msgid ""
"Prosecutes the case against the work: steelmanned opposing positions, the "
"argument's weakest links, what would falsify it, and who disagrees and why. "
"Key Arguments maps the argument; this one argues back. Can target a specific "
"section. Result is saved as an artifact."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:1999
msgid ""
"Generates 8-10 discussion questions spanning comprehension, analysis, "
"interpretation, and personal connection. Good for book clubs or classroom "
"use. Can target a specific section. Result is saved as an artifact."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2047
msgid ""
"Interactive comprehension quiz with multiple choice, short answer, and essay "
"questions. Answers one at a time with scoring. Result is saved as an "
"artifact. Can be triggered automatically at chapter ends."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2076
msgid "Document Analysis"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2077
msgid ""
"Analyzes the document's thesis, structure, key insights, and audience. The "
"result is saved as an Analyze artifact that other actions can reference. Can "
"target a specific section."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2111
msgid "Document Summary"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2112
msgid ""
"Creates a comprehensive summary preserving key details and structure. The "
"result is saved as a Summary artifact, which other actions can use as their "
"document source. Can target a specific section."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2138
msgid "Extract Key Insights"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2139
msgid ""
"Distills the most important takeaways: ideas worth remembering, novel "
"perspectives, actionable conclusions, and connections to broader concepts. "
"Can target a specific section. Result is saved as an artifact."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2176
msgid ""
"A spoiler-free guide to what's ahead: themes developing, questions worth "
"holding, patterns to notice. Uses your reading position to stay safe. Can "
"target a specific section."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2223
msgid "Suggest from Library"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2224
msgid ""
"Suggests what to read next from your own library, based on the current book "
"and your reading history."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2228 prompts/actions.lua:2380 prompts/actions.lua:2397
#: prompts/actions.lua:2413 prompts/actions.lua:2430
msgid ""
"Enable library scanning in Settings → Privacy & Data to use this action."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2245
msgid "Reviews"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2246
msgid ""
"Searches the web for critical and reader reviews, awards, and any "
"controversy about the work."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2281
msgid "Compare"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2282
msgid ""
"Compares the selected works, focusing on meaningful contrasts: different "
"approaches, unique strengths, and which readers would prefer which."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2293
msgid "Find Common Themes"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2294
msgid ""
"Identifies shared themes, intellectual traditions, and deeper patterns "
"across the selected works: beyond surface-level genre labels."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2305
msgid "Analyze Collection"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2306
msgid ""
"Analyzes what the collection reveals about the reader's interests, "
"perspective, and what might be missing for a more complete picture."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2318
msgid "Quick Summaries"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2319
msgid ""
"A brief 2-3 sentence summary of each selected work, focusing on premise and "
"appeal."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2330
msgid "Reading Order"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2331
msgid ""
"Suggests an optimal reading order based on conceptual dependencies, "
"difficulty progression, and thematic arc."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2342
msgid "Recommend"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2343
msgid ""
"Recommends 5-8 new works based on the patterns across your selected works: "
"matching the intersection of your interests, not just similarity to one "
"title. When library scanning is enabled, notes which recommendations you "
"already own and prioritizes books you haven't read."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2356
msgid ""
"Analyzes your highlights, annotations, and notes across the selected books: "
"what patterns emerge in what you mark, what you write, and how your thinking "
"connects across works."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2360
msgid ""
"Enable highlights or annotations sharing in Settings → Privacy & Data to use "
"this action."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2373
msgid "Next Read"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2374
msgid ""
"Suggests what to read next from your library: including books worth "
"revisiting or picking back up. Based on what you've finished recently, "
"what's been sitting unread, and your reading patterns. When advanced stats "
"are enabled, includes engagement context like books you've stalled on or "
"read extensively."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2390
msgid "Discover New"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2391
msgid ""
"Suggests new books based on your library: identifies your taste from what "
"you own and recommends works you don't have yet, including a few picks "
"outside your comfort zone. When advanced stats are enabled, uses engagement "
"data to better understand your preferences."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2406
msgid "Analyze Library"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2407
msgid ""
"Analyzes your library to reveal genres and authors you gravitate toward, "
"completion patterns, and gaps in your collection. When advanced stats are "
"enabled, includes engagement insights like which books you spent the most "
"time on."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2423
msgid "Challenge My Taste"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2424
msgid ""
"Critiques your reading pattern rather than celebrating it: where your "
"library is one-sided, which voices are missing, and what a sharp critic of "
"your shelf would say: ending with a few books that would argue with it. When "
"advanced stats are enabled, includes engagement patterns."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2444
msgid "News Update"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2445
msgid ""
"Fetches today's top global news stories from Al Jazeera with headlines, "
"summaries, and links. Uses web search."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2474
msgid ""
"Translates the selected text into your configured translation language. This "
"action also controls the Translate Current Page function."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2494
msgid "Quick Define"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2495
msgid ""
"A brief, one-line dictionary definition of the selected word in your "
"dictionary language."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2528
msgid ""
"Full dictionary entry with pronunciation, definitions, etymology, and "
"synonyms."
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2561
msgid "Deep Analysis"
msgstr ""

#: prompts/actions.lua:2562
msgid ""
"Deep linguistic analysis covering morphology, word family, etymology, "
"cognates, and cross-language borrowings. Adapts to the word's language "
"family (Semitic roots, Indo-European stems, etc.)."
msgstr ""
